@startuml Integral Computation

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActivityBorderColor Black
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFFDD
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999

title Integral Computation Phase
caption All integrals are **identical** for RHF, UHF, and ROHF — they depend only on geometry and basis set.

' ============================================================
' START – Input from Initialization
' ============================================================
start

:▲ **Input** (from Initialization):
• Molecule – atomic positions <latex>\{\mathbf{R}_A\}</latex> in Bohr, nuclear charges <latex>\{Z_A\}</latex>
• **cgto** – flat list of CGTO shells <latex>\{\phi_\mu\}</latex>
  (lazy property, built on first access via Molecule)
  each carrying <latex>(\mathbf{R}_A,\, l,\, \{\alpha_p\},\, \{d_p\})</latex>
  and contributing <latex>2l + 1</latex> basis functions
• **n_basis** – total number of basis functions (sum of <latex>2l+1</latex> over all shells)
• HF method tag (RHF / UHF / ROHF) — **not used** in this phase; <<#LightCyan>>

note right
    Each CGTO is a fixed linear combination
    of primitive Gaussians:
    <latex>\phi_\mu(\mathbf{r}) = \sum_{p} d_{p\mu}\, g_{p}(\alpha_{p\mu},\, \mathbf{r} - \mathbf{R}_\mu)</latex>
    where <latex>g_p</latex> is a Cartesian Gaussian primitive
    with exponent <latex>\alpha_{p\mu}</latex> and contraction
    coefficient <latex>d_{p\mu}</latex>.
end note

!startsub INTEGRAL_COMPUTATION
partition "Integral Computation" {

    ' ============================================================
    ' ONE-ELECTRON INTEGRALS (parallel, independent)
    ' ============================================================
    fork
        partition "Overlap Matrix  S" {
            :Compute **Overlap Matrix** <latex>\mathbf{S}</latex>
            <latex>S_{\mu\nu} = \langle\phi_\mu | \phi_\nu\rangle = \int \phi_\mu(\mathbf{r})\, \phi_\nu(\mathbf{r})\, d\mathbf{r}</latex>

            Dimension: <latex>n_{basis} \times n_{basis}</latex>
            Properties: symmetric, positive-definite
            Algorithm: McMurchie-Davidson recursion; <<#LightCyan>>

            note right
                Measures non-orthogonality
                of the AO basis.
                <latex>S_{\mu\mu} = 1</latex> (normalized),
                <latex>0 \le S_{\mu\nu} \le 1</latex>.
            end note
        }

    fork again
        partition "Kinetic Energy Matrix  T" {
            :Compute **Kinetic Energy Matrix** <latex>\mathbf{T}</latex>
            <latex>T_{\mu\nu} = \langle\phi_\mu| -\tfrac{1}{2}\nabla^2 |\phi_\nu\rangle = -\frac{1}{2}\int \phi_\mu(\mathbf{r})\, \nabla^2 \phi_\nu(\mathbf{r})\, d\mathbf{r}</latex>

            Dimension: <latex>n_{basis} \times n_{basis}</latex>
            Properties: symmetric, positive semi-definite
            Algorithm: McMurchie-Davidson recursion; <<#LightCyan>>

            note right
                Electron kinetic energy
                in atomic units
                (<latex>\hbar = m_e = 1</latex>).
            end note
        }

    fork again
        partition "Nuclear Attraction Matrix  V" {
            :Compute **Nuclear Attraction Matrix** <latex>\mathbf{V}</latex>
            <latex>V_{\mu\nu} = \sum_{A}^{N_{atoms}} \langle\phi_\mu| -\frac{Z_A}{|\mathbf{r}-\mathbf{R}_A|} |\phi_\nu\rangle</latex>
            <latex>= -\sum_{A}^{N_{atoms}} Z_A \int \phi_\mu(\mathbf{r})\, \frac{1}{|\mathbf{r}-\mathbf{R}_A|}\, \phi_\nu(\mathbf{r})\, d\mathbf{r}</latex>

            Dimension: <latex>n_{basis} \times n_{basis}</latex>
            Properties: symmetric, negative semi-definite
            Algorithm: McMurchie-Davidson + Boys function; <<#LightCyan>>

            note right
                Coulomb attraction between
                each electron and every
                nucleus. Uses the Boys
                function <latex>F_n(x)</latex> for the
                <latex>1/r</latex> integrals over Gaussians.
            end note
        }

    end fork

    ' ============================================================
    ' CORE HAMILTONIAN
    ' ============================================================
    :Assemble **Core Hamiltonian**
    <latex>\mathbf{H}^{core} = \mathbf{T} + \mathbf{V}</latex>

    This is the complete one-electron Hamiltonian
    (kinetic energy + nuclear attraction).
    Dimension: <latex>n_{basis} \times n_{basis}</latex>; <<#LightCyan>>

    ' ============================================================
    ' TWO-ELECTRON INTEGRALS (ERI)
    ' ============================================================
    :Compute **Two-Electron Repulsion Integrals** (ERI tensor)
    <latex>(\mu\nu|\lambda\sigma) = \iint \phi_\mu(\mathbf{r}_1)\, \phi_\nu(\mathbf{r}_1)\, \frac{1}{|\mathbf{r}_1 - \mathbf{r}_2|}\, \phi_\lambda(\mathbf{r}_2)\, \phi_\sigma(\mathbf{r}_2)\, d\mathbf{r}_1\, d\mathbf{r}_2</latex>

    Chemist notation: <latex>(\mu\nu|\lambda\sigma)</latex>
    Dimension: <latex>n_{basis}^4</latex> unique index combinations
    (reduced by 8-fold permutational symmetry)
    Algorithm: McMurchie-Davidson + Boys function; <<#LightCyan>>

    note right
        **Permutational symmetries** of the ERI tensor:
        <latex>(\mu\nu|\lambda\sigma) = (\nu\mu|\lambda\sigma) = (\mu\nu|\sigma\lambda) = (\nu\mu|\sigma\lambda)</latex>
        <latex>= (\lambda\sigma|\mu\nu) = (\sigma\lambda|\mu\nu) = (\lambda\sigma|\nu\mu) = (\sigma\lambda|\nu\mu)</latex>

        Only <latex>\sim n_{basis}^4/8</latex> unique integrals
        need to be computed and stored.
    end note

    ' ============================================================
    ' NUCLEAR REPULSION ENERGY
    ' ============================================================
    :Compute **Nuclear Repulsion Energy**
    <latex>E_{nuc} = \sum_{A < B}^{N_{atoms}} \frac{Z_A\, Z_B}{|\mathbf{R}_A - \mathbf{R}_B|}</latex>

    Classical point-charge Coulomb repulsion.
    This is a scalar constant (no electron dependence).; <<#LightCyan>>
}
!endsub

' ============================================================
' NOTE – Method independence
' ============================================================
note right
    **No RHF / UHF / ROHF branching in this phase.**
    All integrals <latex>\mathbf{S}, \mathbf{T}, \mathbf{V},</latex>
    <latex>(\mu\nu|\lambda\sigma)</latex>, and <latex>E_{nuc}</latex> are
    determined **solely** by the molecular geometry
    and the basis set. Method-specific logic begins
    in SCF Initialization and SCF Iteration Loop.
end note

' ============================================================
' END – Output to downstream phases
' ============================================================
:▼ **Output** (passed to subsequent phases):
• <latex>\mathbf{S}</latex>  (<latex>n_{basis} \times n_{basis}</latex>)  → SCF Initialization, SCF Iteration Loop, Post-SCF Analysis
• <latex>\mathbf{H}^{core}</latex>  (<latex>n_{basis} \times n_{basis}</latex>)  → SCF Initialization, SCF Iteration Loop
• ERI tensor  (<latex>\sim n_{basis}^4/8</latex> unique values)  → SCF Iteration Loop
• <latex>E_{nuc}</latex>  (scalar)  → Finalization (<latex>E_{total} = E_{elec} + E_{nuc}</latex>); <<#LightCyan>>

stop

' ============================================================
' LEGEND
' ============================================================
legend right
    **Index Notation:**
    |= Index |= Range |= Description |
    | μ, ν, λ, σ | 1 … n_basis | Basis function indices |
    | p | 1 … K | Primitive Gaussian index within a contraction |
    | A, B | 1 … N_atoms | Atom indices |
    | i | 1 … n_basis | Molecular orbital index |
    ----
    **Symbol Legend:**
    |= Symbol |= Description |
    | φ_μ(**r**) | Contracted Gaussian-type orbital (CGTO) basis function |
    | g_p | Primitive Cartesian Gaussian |
    | d_p | Contraction coefficient of primitive p |
    | α_p | Gaussian exponent of primitive p |
    | K | Number of primitives in a CGTO (contraction length) |
    | l | Angular momentum quantum number (0=s, 1=p, 2=d, …) |
    | l_x, l_y, l_z | Cartesian angular momentum components (l_x + l_y + l_z = l) |
    | **r** | Arbitrary evaluation point (CartesianCoordinates) |
    | **R**_A | Position of atom A / CGTO centre (in Bohr) |
    | Z_A | Atomic number (nuclear charge) of atom A |
    | n_basis | Total number of basis functions |
    | N_atoms | Total number of atoms in the molecule |
    ----
    **Matrix/Integral Symbols:**
    |= Symbol |= Description |
    | **S** | Overlap matrix – S_μν = ⟨φ_μ|φ_ν⟩ |
    | **T** | Kinetic energy matrix – T_μν = ⟨φ_μ|−½∇²|φ_ν⟩ |
    | **V** | Nuclear attraction matrix – electron-nucleus Coulomb |
    | **H**^core | Core Hamiltonian – **T** + **V** |
    | (μν|λσ) | Two-electron repulsion integral (ERI) in chemist notation |
    | E_nuc | Nuclear repulsion energy – classical Coulomb between nuclei |
    | F_n(x) | Boys function – auxiliary for Coulomb integrals over Gaussians |
    | McMurchie-Davidson | Efficient recursion scheme for Gaussian integral evaluation |
    ----
    **Note:** This phase is **method-independent.**
    RHF, UHF, and ROHF all compute the same set
    of integrals. Method-specific logic begins
    in the SCF Initialization phase.
    ----
    **HF Method Colors (for reference):**
    |<#LightGreen> RHF | Restricted Closed-Shell |
    |<#LightCoral> UHF | Unrestricted |
    |<#LightYellow> ROHF | Restricted Open-Shell |
endlegend

@enduml
